R-11 determination and TCS-02 §5 live telemetry are on file.\n\nSee Municipal_Witness_Test_Package.docx Rev 1 (DER Program Office, 07/14/2025).	2025-07-24	\N	1	11	9	\N	4	1	\N	\N	2026-11-20 12:00:30.009202+00	2026-11-20 13:39:48.251007+00	2025-07-15	\N	\N	1	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	8	f	\N	\N	\N
49	1	3	Schedule witness test — Lockmere Middle (actual installed Selvix SV-720)	Witness test required under ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §4.1 because the inverter actually installed at Lockmere Middle is a Selvix SV-720 (commissioning wiki file note by Evan Solberg, comment 15), not the Torvane Electric TE-180K shown on the submitted checklist. Selvix SV-720 is not carried on CEL-2025-Q2; it appears only on the superseded CEL-2024-Q4 (Inverters row 29). The checklist's TE-180K listing therefore cannot support a waiver.\n\nScope: IEEE 1547.1 testing per ENG-PRC-014 §4.2 against the actual Selvix SV-720 and its approved settings: protective-function trip tests, anti-islanding test (method actually installed; if passive-only, the DPS-07 §4.5 study), Category II voltage/frequency ride-through verifications, and revalidation of 27/59, 81U/81O, 25, 32 and reclose-block settings. The checklist records a POI recloser with reclose-block interlocked to the DER breaker, so the full DPS-07 Rev 2 §6.2 site-acceptance set applies, including item 1 insulation-resistance/dielectric, item 2 CT/VT ratio-polarity-burden, ANSI 79 automatic reclosing in its issued enabled/blocked state, item 4 end-to-end trip through the recloser interrupter, item 5 local/remote control-status-metering, item 6 synchronism check and reclose-block logic, and item 7 visible-break/lockout. Customer/commissioning agent performs with calibrated instrumentation and qualified personnel; the Alleniom Standards Engineering witness engineer observes, records and signs the test record; Distribution Protection Engineering issues the §6.3 written acceptance.\n\nProposed test date: 07/29/2025. Reserve date: 08/05/2025. Prerequisites due 07/22/2025: corrected checklist and as-built documentation showing actual Selvix SV-720 model, serial and firmware; revised single-line/equipment schedule; approved protection settings sheet for the actual equipment; anti-islanding method statement / DPS-07 §4.5 study; IEEE 1547.1 test plan; instrument calibration certificates; qualified personnel; manufacturer certificate/factory test report or equivalent; POI recloser factory acceptance records (DPS-07 §6.1); and AHJ re-inspection or written confirmation that permit BE-2025-0148 covers the installed Selvix SV-720 (the substitution post-dates the 06/09/2025 sign-off). No PTO until the signed witness record, the ER-11/recloser determination, the AHJ reconciliation and TCS-02 §5 live telemetry are on file.\n\nSee Municipal_Witness_Test_Package.docx Rev 1 (DER Program Office, 07/14/2025).	2025-07-29	\N	1	11	9	\N	4	1	\N	\N	2026-11-20 12:00:31.655022+00	2026-11-20 13:39:49.700821+00	2025-07-15	\N	\N	1	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	11	f	\N	\N	\N
45	1	3	Process the municipal witness-test waiver batch	Six municipal arrays have submitted commissioning checklists pre-marked as waiver eligible. Determine each array's actual waiver eligibility and schedule whatever the outcome requires before PTO. Tresbay Community Center withdrew its request on 07/09/2025 and is out of this batch.\n\nBATCH DETERMINATION — 07/14/2025 (package Rev 1)\nSix checklists reviewed (Cravenwood High, Darnwick Elementary, Holcott Library, Lockmere Middle, Marden Falls WRF, Tresbay Community Center). Tresbay withdrew 07/09/2025 and is out of the batch; five arrays remain in scope.\nCurrent CEL for the determination: CEL-2025-Q2 (published 04/30/2025; CEL-2025-Q3 planned 07/31/2025, not in force on 07/14/2025).\nCarried on CEL-2025-Q2: Cravenwood High — Solmery Power SM-215K-3P (Inverters row 6; 215 kW; UL 1741-SB); Marden Falls WRF — Solmery Power SM-245K-3P (Inverters row 7; 245 kW; UL 1741-SB).\nNot carried: Darnwick Elementary — Arvexa PV-750 (not on CEL-2025-Q2 or any current tab); Holcott Library — Selvix SV-720 (only on superseded CEL-2024-Q4, Inverters row 29); Lockmere Middle — actual installed inverter Selvix SV-720 per commissioning wiki file note (checklist incorrectly shows Torvane Electric TE-180K; SV-720 not on CEL-2025-Q2).\nWitness tests required: Darnwick Elementary, Holcott Library, Lockmere Middle. Scheduling items: WP #47 (Holcott, proposed 07/22/2025), WP #48 (Darnwick, proposed 07/24/2025), WP #49 (Lockmere, proposed 07/29/2025). Witness scope carries the full DPS-07 Rev 2 §6.2 site-acceptance set (items 1–2 insulation-resistance/dielectric and CT/VT verification; ANSI 79 reclosing where a POI recloser is installed), the DPS-07 §4.5 anti-islanding basis, and the unconditional Lockmere AHJ reconciliation (the substitution post-dates the 06/09/2025 sign-off).\nSOC release list as of 07/14/2025: NO ARRAY. Marden Falls WRF is the only candidate — carried on the current CEL and telemetry recorded end-to-end with the SOC, but its waiver is unsigned (ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §4.3), no Form ER-11 determination on the DPS-07 §4.2 POI-recloser question is on file, and its RTU model/asset and transport are not recorded (TCS-02 §3.2/§4.1). Release only when those close and the SOC confirms live telemetry at PTO. Cravenwood is carried but telemetry is pending. Lockmere has live telemetry but requires a witness test. Darnwick and Holcott require both.\nWaiver disposition remains reserved to Standards Engineering. Package: Municipal_Witness_Test_Package.docx Rev 1, filed in /DER_Program/Commissioning/Municipal.\nClosure condition: the three scheduling items standing on this case are exactly the three arrays whose determination is "witness test required"; the case is closed on that agreement as of 07/14/2025.	2025-08-15	\N	12	11	9	5	4	3	100	\N	2026-11-20 11:41:45.45569+00	2026-11-20 13:39:18.891999+00	2025-06-27	\N	\N	1	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	36	f	\N	\N	\N
